infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title No index vs one B-tree index
  desc Same query on 10M rows — an index buys read speed by taxing every write and the disk
  compares
    - label Sequential scan (no index)
      children
        - label ~2s per query
          desc WHERE user_id = 42 touches every one of the 10M rows
        - label No write overhead
          desc INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE touch only the table
        - label No extra storage
          desc Nothing to keep in sync on disk
    - label Index scan (one B-tree)
      children
        - label ~3ms per query
          desc O(log n) tree walk then heap fetch — a 600x speedup
        - label 5-50 us per write
          desc Every write to the indexed column must update the index too
        - label +10-30% of table size
          desc A separate sorted on-disk structure per index
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
